Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 06:33:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(otp): store HMACs, CSPRNG codes, per-phone lockout,
 atomic consume

- otp_codes.code now holds HMAC-SHA256(OTP_PEPPER|SESSION_SECRET,
  phone:code), compared with timingSafeEqual; plaintext never stored.
- Codes come from crypto.randomInt instead of Math.random.
- A new code expires the previous active codes for that phone.
- 5 failed verifications for a phone expire its active codes (the
  per-IP limiter did not stop distributed guessing).
- Codes are consumed atomically (verified=false in the UPDATE).
- Throwaway passwords for OTP-created users use crypto.randomBytes.

